messages:
maria: Heads-up — opened a docs PR (gh#4521) for function-calling + structured-output migration. Main asks: 1) canonical example shape we recommend (envelope vs top-level), 2) add short Python/Node SDK snippets for the new shape, 3) fix a few broken anchor links in the site. :eyes:
aj: Link? can you paste the PR and the specific anchor errors?
maria: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4521 — anchors that currently break on build: /docs/tool-calling#schema-example -> should be /docs/tool-calling#schema-example-ids; /docs/structured-output#json-shape -> header id changed during last reorg. I listed them in the PR description.
sam: I skimmed — example section currently shows both the raw JSON Schema and a compact envelope. Folks on Slack asked for a parse-fallback snippet too (how to graceful-handle older agent outputs).
laura: I can add Node + TS snippet for the new SDK shape. Quick question: do we prefer the envelope pattern by default? i.e. {"envelope": {"tool":..., "args":...}} vs top-level tool fields.
jon: Recommend envelope for forward compatibility (we can add metadata later). But include a top-level compatibility example and a brief migration note. Also call out nullable arrays — common gotcha.
aj: also: site build fails when anchor text includes backticks and parens. fixing the header ids to stable kebab-case will reduce breakage.
maria: Plan: we pick envelope as canonical, add compat example + parse-fallback snippet, and run a linkfix PR to replace old anchors with stable ids. Volunteers?
sam: I can run a grep+replace across the built HTML and the Markdown sources, open a tiny PR that replaces those anchors with the new ids, and add a short test in our link-checker job. Estimated ~30m.
laura: I'll add SDK snippets into docs/clients/python.md and docs/clients/node.md on branch docs/toolcall-shape-migration. Will include: 1) generate call with envelope, 2) parse-fallback helper for older top-level responses. Pushing later today.
maria: awesome. For the migration blurb I propose this copy (short):
```
If your integration parsed top-level tool fields, switch to the envelope pattern to avoid future breaking changes. To maintain compatibility, use the provided parseFallback() helper which accepts both envelope and legacy shapes.
```
jon: LGTM. Can you also add a tiny JSON Schema example for the envelope shape to the docs? Something minimal so folks can copy/paste.
maria: here's a tiny schema I drafted — please review: 
```
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "envelope": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "tool": {"type": "string"},
        "args": {"type": "object"}
      },
      "required": ["tool", "args"]
    }
  },
  "required": ["envelope"]
}
```
laura: I'll include that under the examples section and also add a compact runner snippet for Node: 
```
// Node pseudo-code with new SDK
const res = await client.generate({
  input: `Call tool`,
  structured_output: {
    schema: ENVELOPE_SCHEMA_ID,
    format: 'json'
  }
});
const parsed = parseFallback(res.text);
if (parsed.envelope) {
  await callTool(parsed.envelope);
}
```
aj: docs-bot just posted a staging deploy — can we run the link check once laura and sam push?
docs-bot: Deploy to staging: successful (env: staging) — link-check job queued.
sam: I'll wait for laura's commit then run link-check locally and push tiny fixes. If anything else shows up I'll tag you @maria.
maria: Thanks everyone. Action items I pulled: 
- laura: SDK snippets + migration blurb on docs/toolcall-shape-migration branch.
- sam: anchor/link fixes + link-check tweak PR.
- jon: quick review of schema + nullable array note (small comment in gh PR).
- aj: follow up on CI flakiness tied to anchor id generation.
I'll merge once link-check is green and we have the snippets. :thumbsup:
laura: will do, aiming this afternoon.
jon: will review after lunch.
docs-bot: Note: CI link-check job will fail PRs that contain unresolved anchors.
